@page "/payment/complete"
@layout BareLayout

<PageTitle>Payment received</PageTitle>

@* Where Accelerate sends a customer after paying when it has no checkout to send them back to: the
   Payments:CallbackUrl fallback (PAYMENT_CALLBACK_URL). Signed out, on a phone, straight from the payment page,
   so it is a plain thank-you with no app chrome, and never the sign-in page (Routes lets /payment/ through).
   It doesn't claim the order is paid: that is the provider's webhook's to say, and the business hears of it from
   the webhook. *@
<main class="payment-complete">
    <section class="payment-complete__card" role="status">
        <span class="payment-complete__icon"><Icon Name="IconName.RiCheckboxCircleFill" Size="IconSize.Lg" /></span>
        <Typography TextStyle="TextStyle.HeadingH3Semibold" As="h1">Thanks for your payment</Typography>
        <Typography TextStyle="TextStyle.BodySmallMedium" As="p" Prose>
            We're confirming it now, and the business is told as soon as it's through.
        </Typography>
        <Typography TextStyle="TextStyle.BodySmallMedium" As="p" Prose>
            You can close this page and go back to the chat. Please don't pay again.
        </Typography>
    </section>
</main>
